    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-3.3.06-01",
      "block_type": "definition",
      "heading": "Urbanisation and environmental change",
      "text": "Urban development changes land cover, demand and waste flows. Effects can include air, water, visual and noise pollution, as well as outward expansion into surrounding land. Their scale depends on consumption, production, infrastructure and management, not population alone. A growing urban share is a demographic measure; an expanded built footprint is a spatial change. They can be linked without being identical.",
      "claim_ids": [
