      "block_id": "BL-6137-3.3.06-02",
      "block_type": "worked_application",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Air pollution can arise from vehicles, industry, burning or other relevant sources. Exposure depends on emissions, weather, location and the people or environments affected. More traffic can contribute under suitable conditions, but a vehicle count alone is not a pollutant concentration. A clear explanation identifies source, pathway and consequence using the resource rather than assigning every respiratory problem to the nearest road.",
