      "block_id": "BL-6137-3.3.06-03",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Urban air management can include appropriate emission controls, cleaner services, reliable public transport or reduced unnecessary journeys. Each targets a pathway and has costs or requirements. Shifting pollution away from one street is not the same as reducing total emissions. Compare the relevant system boundary and service before declaring success. The environmental result needs suitable measurements beyond a plan or equipment purchase.",
      "claim_ids": [
