    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-3.3.06-05",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Pollution can affect people downstream or outside the urban boundary. A city can benefit from activity while other users bear water-treatment costs or ecological damage. Appropriate management therefore includes the receiving environment rather than treating the city limit as the end of the pathway. A visible improvement in one area can coexist with displaced harm if waste is simply transferred unsafely.",
      "claim_ids": [
