    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-3.3.06-06",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Visual pollution concerns an unwanted or damaging effect on appearance or amenity, such as unmanaged litter, derelict sites or unsuitable clutter in a specified context. Judgements can be subjective, so an assessment needs clear indicators and stakeholder perspectives. A difference in building style is not automatically pollution. Define the feature being assessed rather than label an unfamiliar neighbourhood as unattractive without evidence.",
