    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-3.3.06-07",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Noise pollution involves unwanted sound affecting people or other relevant receptors. Traffic, industry, construction and activities can contribute. Effects vary with level, timing, duration and sensitivity. A short sound reading during a special event may not describe normal conditions. Comparisons need matched periods and a suitable method. A management response can address route, timing, design or operation depending on the source.",
