    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-3.3.06-08",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Urban sprawl is outward expansion of the urban built area into surrounding land, often creating more extensive development. It is not simply rural–urban migration or a synonym for informal housing. Formal estates, industry, shopping areas and sports facilities can all contribute to an expanding footprint. Population can become more urban without the exact same pattern of land expansion, so read the spatial evidence separately.",
