    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-3.3.06-09",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Expansion can convert agricultural land or habitats, fragment open space and alter runoff. Longer distances can increase travel needs where development is poorly connected to jobs or services. New facilities may also create employment or improve access for some users. A supported evaluation recognises the specific benefits and costs rather than assuming that all edge development has one effect.",
