    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-3.3.06-11",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Land-use planning can protect sensitive areas, coordinate housing and services or encourage suitable reuse of existing sites. Brownfield redevelopment can reduce pressure for new land in some situations, but remediation, cost and suitability matter. Compact development can shorten some journeys while requiring adequate open space, services and affordable access. No single density or design removes all environmental and social trade-offs.",
