    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-3.3.06-12",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "A teaching before-and-after plan can show a built area expanding from ten to fifteen square units, replacing five units of surrounding land under a fixed classification. That is a 50% footprint increase. It does not prove a 50% population increase, an exact emissions rise or that all converted land was farmland. Each additional claim needs the relevant population, activity or land-use key.",
