    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-3.3.06-13",
      "block_type": "worked_application",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Environmental assessment should compare matched dates and conditions. Changes in waste collection, industrial operation, rainfall or travel can affect observations independently of population growth. An increase in litter near new housing might reflect inadequate collection capacity rather than residents' supposed attitudes. Identifying the service mechanism helps select a useful response and avoids blaming a group from an aggregate pattern.",
