    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-3.3.06-16",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "A land-cover account needs a fixed classification. Built area expanding from ten to fifteen square units is a five-unit gain relative to an opening ten, or 50%. The surrounding area lost depends on the full boundary and key. If the added area includes former farmland, habitat and vacant land, their individual totals must be read separately. A single total cannot establish that all conversion was agricultural loss.",
      "claim_ids": [
