    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-3.3.06-17",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Hard surfaces can increase rapid runoff where infiltration falls. More water reaches drains or channels quickly, potentially increasing local flood pressure if capacity is inadequate. Suitable drainage, permeable surfaces or protected flow routes can address parts of the mechanism. Their usefulness depends on design, maintenance and storm conditions. A drainage asset that merely transfers polluted water downstream has not established an overall environmental improvement.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "CL-6137-3.3.06-1",
        "CL-6137-3.3.06-2",
