    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-3.3.06-19",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Noise assessment can record comparable locations and times with an appropriate instrument and definition. A perception survey adds information about experience, but respondents can differ in sensitivity or activity. Both forms of evidence can be useful while measuring different things. A quiet daytime reading does not establish acceptable night-time conditions. The management recommendation should match the affected period and source.",
      "claim_ids": [
