    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-3.3.06-20",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Visual assessment similarly needs an operational scale. Observers can record litter, condition of buildings or signage using defined anchors rather than an unexplained personal score. Agreement can be improved through practice, but cultural preferences and site context still matter. A low score should describe the chosen indicators, not judge the worth of residents. This keeps environmental-quality work both interpretable and respectful.",
      "claim_ids": [
