    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-3.3.06-22",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Reusing existing land can reduce one pressure while introducing others. A former industrial site may need remediation before housing is suitable; a compact development may need additional school or water capacity. A greenfield site may be cheaper initially while converting habitat or productive soil. The evaluation should include the stated costs and environmental pathways over time rather than treat a category name as a complete verdict.",
