      "block_type": "worked_application",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "A good urban-environment conclusion can therefore be conditional and specific. If sewage treatment and collection expand to meet usable needs, some pollution risks can decline despite population growth. If demand rises while services fail, pressure can worsen. The relationship is mediated by infrastructure, behaviour and resources. Identifying that mechanism supports useful responses instead of blaming a population total alone.",
